{"schema_version":1,"stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a11814-393b-7672-9cf2-d8be248ebf2c"},"sequence":87,"recorded_at":1791405349338602,"payload_type":"runtime.session","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run","run_id":"2a49c4f6-785b-4ab4-b29f-48271c0594c3","event":{"kind":"reasoning_summary_committed","message_id":"fed8d420-f767-4825-9b16-9ba844159574","response_id":"resp_6ac6ad2261c77aa59df54b97","text":"Summarizing Supabase RLS enablement steps, policy creation, security checklist, Data API grants, and schema change approach.","provider_item_id":"rs_6ac6ad2261c77aa59df54b97:rs_01a118144d0a73e692f35af450e729ab"},"source_run_record_id":"35f960dc-4126-48f3-a73b-73fb2ef165c8","source_run_record_sequence":35}}
{"schema_version":1,"stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a11814-393b-7672-9cf2-d8be248ebf2c"},"sequence":89,"recorded_at":1791405350739297,"payload_type":"runtime.session","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run","run_id":"2a49c4f6-785b-4ab4-b29f-48271c0594c3","event":{"kind":"assistant_message_committed","message_id":"fbd444c3-bcd8-41d6-9c4f-ce1e227ea410","response_id":"resp_6ac6ad2261c77aa59df54b97","text":"Enable RLS, then add policies — enabling alone blocks all Data API access until a policy allows it:\n\n```sql\nalter table public.your_table enable row level security;\n\ncreate policy \"select_own\"\non public.your_table for select\nto authenticated\nusing ( (select auth.uid()) = user_id );\n```\n\nNotes per Supabase guidance:\n\n* Do this for every table in an exposed schema (`public` by default). If you created the table via SQL and it's inaccessible, also check Data API exposure / `GRANT`s to `anon`/`authenticated` — that's separate from RLS.\n* Don't use deprecated `auth.role() = 'authenticated'` — use `TO authenticated` / `TO anon`.\n* `UPDATE` needs a `SELECT` policy first, plus both `USING` and `WITH CHECK`:\n\n```sql\ncreate policy \"update_own\"\non public.your_table for update\nto authenticated\nusing ( (select auth.uid()) = user_id )\nwith check ( (select auth.uid()) = user_id );\n```\n\nDashboard alternative: Table Editor > select table > Enable RLS, then add policies under Authentication > Policies.\n\nAfter changing: run `supabase db advisors` and test with an authenticated query to confirm allowed rows return and denied rows don't.\n","provider_item_id":"msg_01a1181459c073cfa17b31efb1971778"},"source_run_record_id":"016765b0-a9e1-4fa0-a4c7-0b079eba8e97","source_run_record_sequence":95}}
